From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:17:01 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] feat(sim_display): XRT_SIM_DISPLAY_FULL_SBS_ONLY, a build
 with 2D and full side by side only

For a distribution whose desktop compositor makes every display format from
one full side-by-side picture (Sparky Stereo OS with Stereo KWin): with the
option ON, sim_display offers two rendering modes, 2D and Full SBS (mode 1,
the default), and the anaglyph, cropped and squeezed SBS, quad, blend and
interlaced outputs are not built (their shaders are not compiled and their
pipelines are not created). SIM_DISPLAY_OUTPUT accepts sbs_full and 2d and
logs why it keeps sbs_full for any other value. With a zone mask active,
full side by side is drawn as it is and the log says so, since there is no
anaglyph to substitute. The option is OFF by default; nothing changes for
other builds apart from creating the pipelines from the shaders that were
built (all of them when OFF).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Origin: vendor, Sparky Stereo OS ORDER 58
Forwarded: not-needed
Comment: The edition builds sim_display with XRT_SIM_DISPLAY_FULL_SBS_ONLY=ON: its one stereo output
 is full side by side, declared to Stereo KWin, whose outputs make every display format.
 DisplayXR's own builds keep every output; the option is OFF by default.
Last-Update: 2026-11-07
